      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "That could maybe work for liltoon, but poiyomi is essentially designed against this idea, particularly \"locking shaders\" is actually required for the custom fallback shader option to work, and also poiyomi will remove unused code sections when locking, so many combinations of options. I don't know how efficient it is a run time (I just trust the process), but it means poiyomi using avatars take a long time to first build.\n\nThe main issue with delta patches is that you have to compress the asset bundle in a less efficient manner to have delta patches actually work. Right now the bundles are compressed in a way that prioritize file size over being comparable. \n\nBut yeah, AppImages need to be build to support those delta updates",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
