  "details": "With Avatars 4.0 hinted at, let's take advantage to add Delt Patching: Updating only the files that need to be patched instead of the entire asset bundle. In fact, we don't even need to keep in a single bundle. Let's Split the Body (3D mesh, textures, audio, etc) and the Logic (Shaders, Add-ons, GoGo Loco, .mat, animator controllers)\n\nWe don't need to re-upload an entire 80MB to 150MB asset bundle every time an avatar is updated. VRChat should implement Delta Patching for more efficient asset updating and bandwidth savings. This can allow creators to update their avatars faster and spend fewer resources on updating. Splitting what needs to by updated by the packages AKA Github style updating\n\nThe Current Problem is that for every minor tweak or update, you need to update the E TIRE avatar asset bundle. This is a waste of time and resources for both the player and the bandwidth costs. This is even worse when a shader or avatar addon needs to be manually updated across EVERY avatar. \n\n- Shaders have to manually be updated when they break over time\n\n- Addons like GoGo Loco also break down\n\n- Sometimes you just remove or add a single item\n\nSolution:\n\nUsing Delta Patching and splitting the bundle, we can update faster, only update what's needed, and even let add-on packages be updated without user input.\n\nThis opens the door to shaders that can even be updated without the creator's input. Omega and Baked Shaders (like Silent's cell shader) can updated by the developer. A small server side compute can be done on download and saves massive overhead of having to recompress with LZM. Heavy modular shaders, like Poiyomi, already use YAML and template collections. While these are more prone to needing recompiles but, at 2MBs for just the Logic bundle, the compute overhead is far more sustainable than updating with the entire packages with 50+MBs of avatar files\n\nIn Summary, Delta Patching with splitting the avatar bundles between BODY and LOGIC bundles gives creators a faster way to update their avatars without having to constantly deal with long uploads . In some cases, without even having to open Unity or while on a break.",
